WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.580
Years after the peak of his visibility, Tony
Hawk is still around.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.660
At 50, one might think he's slowing down a
bit, easing into a quiet retirement perhaps.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.760
In fact, Hawk is as busy as ever with philanthropy,
conquering the fashion world, and much more.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.360
For a huge swath of kids, teenagers, and savvy
adults at the dawn of the new millennium,

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.530
Tony Hawk defined what it meant to be awesome.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.500
"What I want people to think of me?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.100
I guess I want them to think I'm just like
them.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.460
Which I basically am."

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.300
But today, the man behind the board is as
much into his family as he is into the half-pipe.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.760
His son Riley Hawk was born of his first marriage
in 1992.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.960
"I think at first people thought it was kind
of strange that I was kind of doing the skate

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:42.540
thing too."

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.200
Two more boys, Spencer and Keegan, were born
of his second marriage, and his first daughter,

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.360
Kadence Clover, was born in 2008.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:54.500
Tony Hawk married once again in 2015 and now
lives comfortably in California.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.640
Hawk might be older now, but his love of skating
pervades his home life.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.860
His eldest son Riley has become a celebrated
skateboarder in his own right on his 21st

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:07.890
birthday, Riley went pro and won the Best
Am award within minutes.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.960
Today, he's sponsored by Baker Skateboards
and has become respected as a street-style

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.340
skater, in contrast to his father, one of
the most celebrated vert-style skaters of

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:16.920
all time.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.480
Kadence also pops up regularly on Hawk's Twitter
and Instagram channels, learning the basics

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.860
from the world's most accomplished teacher.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.480
Tony Hawk has become increasingly involved
in charitable work over the years.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:39.020
In 2002, he created the Tony Hawk Foundation,
an organization that facilitates the building

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.300
of public skateparks across the United States.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:46.820
Focusing specifically on the needs of low-income
and otherwise disenfranchised areas, the foundation

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.060
has awarded $7.9 million dollars in funds
to date.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.340
The breadth of the mission is startling.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.980
Every part of the country has been marked
by Hawk's quest to make skating accessible,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.760
respected, and safe in all communities.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:04.420
Recently, Hawk spearheaded a campaign to take
the foundation global with a $50,000 grant

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:09.609
to Skateistan, an organization that works
to bring skating to Cambodia, Afghanistan,

00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:10.420
and South Africa.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.940
In 2015, Hawk told ABC 10 News:

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.020
"Skateboarding's empowering women in Afghanistan,”

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.120
“more than probably any other sport, to
be honest."

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.719
In 2007, Hawk helped found Athletes for Hope,
which fosters connections between the world

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.420
of elite sports and young hopefuls.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.100
More than ten years later, they're still going
strong.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.200
Hawk has been a hot commodity in the entertainment
world for decades.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.900
Over the years, he's played himself on The
Simpsons, appeared in kiddie fare like Rocket

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.280
Power, and taken bit roles in action flicks
like Deck Dogz.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:49.319
Oh, and don't forget his cameo in the 2005
film Lords of Dogtown, where he played an

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.420
astronaut who wipes out on his skateboard.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:57.080
More recently, Hawk popped up on the popular
YouTube hit Epic Meal Time and he even made

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.430
an appearance on Sesame Street back in 2008:

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.940
"How many wheels on a skateboard?"

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.300
"Four wheels on a skateboard."

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.120
"Can you count 'em for me?"

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.900
Also, we would be remiss to mention his star
turn in The Aquabats!

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:08.400
Super Show!

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.440
"Aquabats, what was it like being thrown into
outer space?"

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.140
"We were in outer space?"

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.900
Skate culture has been influencing the fashion
world for a long time.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:26.340
From Avril Lavigne's stylings in the early
2000s to the classic Vans Off The Wall sneakers,

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.320
skating and fashion have always seemed to
go hand in hand.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.480
It was only a matter of time before an actual
skater took that relationship to the next

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:33.980
level.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.720
Tony Hawk did this with the Tony Hawk Signature
Line, a collection he debuted at Paris Fashion

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.220
Week.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:44.800
The line is an upscale take on skater style,
as envisioned by one of the skating subculture's

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.200
most legendary heroes.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:51.560
Talking to Vogue, Hawk weighed in on the success
of streetwear brands like Palace and Supreme,

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.000
noting how they're now being

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:56.000
"... recognized and embraced by a much bigger
crowd.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.640
People who want to have that look but who
don't necessarily skate."

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.760
In 2019, he told Highsnobiety:

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.540
"If we've reached that level, I want to join
in, too, 'cuz I feel like I have enough to

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.100
offer and I have enough history."

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.240
Hawk's career coincided with the rise of the
internet, so it makes sense that he would

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.159
jump head-first into the world of original
video content.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:19.260
"This is my first skateboard ever and we are
sending it today to the Smithsonian.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.500
And I thought I would give it one last try."

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:26.259
Enter the RIDE channel, Hawk's own little
corner of YouTube, which he launched in 2011.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:29.740
Here, you can immerse yourself in all things
skating and skate culture.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.580
As Hawk says in the welcome video:

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.800
"We're super excited.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:36.660
This is something that we've always wanted
to do and it's finally a reality and it's

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.940
here on YouTube and you should go subscribe
right now."

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.040
RIDE has a dizzying lineup of programs.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.760
There's Concrete Dreams, a documentary web-series
about the challenges of skatepark advocacy.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.860
And there's lots of nitty-gritty reviews for
the latest skating gear.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.389
"If you prefer, like, a slimmer shoe that
you don't have to hold like this, then you

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:56.320
probably shouldn't get these."

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.740
What makes the channel so great?

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.699
It's not about the cool factor; it's about
the reality of the sport.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.280
"We're gonna learn some stuff here and check
out the session and then I'm gonna kick everyone

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:06.780
out."

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.000
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.120
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:16.440
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

